From 5e22de7c2e203be990dae9ae25b1578e5b499dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:59:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): probe on a machine with an inverted X/Y axis
 (Fanuc)

The engine's inverted-axis translation (post::invert) now mirrors the
probing records too, for a script that declares the new manifest flag
probeAxisInversion = true: a TOUCH's target and expected trip, a
RETREAT's incremental delta and nominal end, and each FOUND axis's
expected value negate on the inverted axis. The script's trip read
(#5061..), deviation (found - expected) and G10 L2 write then run in the
controller's frame, where the work offset holds the part datum negated
on that axis, so the correction written is the physical one.

Only fanuc.cps declares the flag. Haas (motion verified, probing hooks
still in draft PR #360) refuses probing on an inverted axis by name;
every script without axisInversion keeps refusing the whole machine.

Proved by the new inverted_probe suite: a test-only Fanuc macro B
controller (tests/macro_b: G0/G1 swept for collisions, G31 tripping on a
simulated part, G90/G91, G54..G59 registers, G10 L2, # arithmetic with
brackets/ABS/unary minus, IF..THEN/GOTO, #3000/#3006) runs the posted
face/edge/corner/bore/boss programs on standard, inverted-X, -Y and -XY
machines with the part shifted off the model: G55 ends at the physical
datum in controller coordinates. A part out of reach alarms no contact;
one past tolerance alarms; the standard-sign program and a translation
missing any one probing word fail. Reads both #377 deviation forms.

Refs #392

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
